# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# The superseded first build, kept for reference. Nothing imports it.
# Listed here so Tailwind v4's source scan skips it — it was scanning
# _old's JSX and emitting 40KB of CSS for classes no live component uses.
/_old

# Superseded and unused source images. They stay on disk but out of git —
# 100 files, 54MB, which is 88% of what the repo would otherwise weigh, and
# anything committed here could only be removed by rewriting shared history.
/public/img/unused images/

# SUPERSEDED SOURCE ART, same reasoning as the folder above and the same
# precedent. Every one of these is the multi-megabyte original that a shipped
# .webp was made from — the seven story photographs, the two background plates,
# the drink and snack stills. 36MB across twenty files, none of them referenced
# by a single line of code, and everything under public/ is SERVED, so they
# would ship to production as well as sit in history forever. They stay on disk
# next to the webps they produced.
/public/img/2019.png
/public/img/2020.png
/public/img/2021.png
/public/img/2022–2023.png
/public/img/2024.png
/public/img/2025.png
/public/img/2026.png
/public/img/badam milk slider.png
/public/img/banana chips.png
/public/img/biscuits.png
/public/img/choclate cofee sldier.png
/public/img/coffee slider.png
/public/img/murukku.png
/public/img/our story bg image.png
/public/img/pantry bg image.png
/public/img/samosa.png
/public/img/tea silder.png
/public/img/tiffin-lid.png
/public/img/tiffin-tier.png
/public/img/vada.png

# Playwright MCP scratch — screenshots and console logs from browser checks.
.playwright-mcp/

# The source PNG for /who-we-serve's hero portrait, same reasoning as the
# block above: 1494KB, superseded by public/img/who-hero-woman.webp at 71KB,
# and it sat at the root of public/ where it would have been served as well
# as stored. Kept on disk next to the webp it produced.
/public/woman.png

# The admin panel's content store. RUNTIME STATE, NOT SOURCE — it is written by
# a form on a running server, so committing it would mean every deploy's
# `git pull` either conflicts with the client's edits or reverts them. The
# versioned copy of these values is DEFAULT_CONTENT in lib/content/schema.ts,
# which is what the site renders when this file is absent.
/data/content.json

# Pictures uploaded through the admin panel. RUNTIME STATE, like the content
# store beside it: written by a form on a running server, so committing them
# would mean every deploy either conflicting with the client's uploads or
# reverting them. The pictures that ship with the build live in public/img and
# are committed; these are not. Back them up the way you would a database.
/public/uploads/*
!/public/uploads/.gitkeep

# Source images for the admin panel, kept on disk and out of the repository —
# the same rule as /public/woman.png above and the PNG block before it: the
# optimised file that the build actually references is committed, the original
# it was made from is not.
#
#   side.png, pv.png, app/adminbg.png  — dropped in while the sidebar and its
#     background were being tried out. Nothing imports any of them.
#   /public/img/sidebar-bg.png         — 692KB, superseded by the 188KB webp
#     beside it, which is what Shell.tsx loads.
#
# Together they are 3.1MB of binaries that no code path reaches. They stay
# where they are; git just does not carry them.
/side.png
/pv.png
/app/adminbg.png
/public/img/sidebar-bg.png
